Observed (facts): after kexec (Q12 from a quiesced source, Q15 from a storming B0 resident) every non-secured bank reaches ctx_probe with SCTLR=0xe7 (M|TRE|AFE|CFRE|CFIE|CFCFG) and the previous kernel's TTBR0 with ASID = bank's DT ASID in bits [55:48] (1e24000 cb4 -> 0x04). FSR=0x200 in every kexec row: bit 9 (FORMAT=LPAE) only, no fault bits, SS (bit 30) clear, so no stalled transaction was inherited even from the storming B0. Cold boot (Q13): SCTLR=0x30000000 (NSCFG only; cb4 also CFCFG), TTBR0=0, FSR=0, i.e. the bootloader leaves the banks disabled. TLBIALL+sync completes in 0.8-5 us per bank (cb4 after kexec ~5 us, cold ~1.5 us). Inference: the same-ASID reuse the patch message describes is exactly what the hardware presents at probe; the probe-time bypass/refill window discussed in the cover is real only for a master still fetching, which this source does not do.

Note: SCTLR reads 0xe7, not the 0x10e7 that init_domain writes: S1_ASIDPNE (bit 12) reads as zero on this SMMU. Not relevant to the fix; recorded for completeness.
